infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Lazy generator pipeline vs eager list materialization
  desc Same 20 GB CSV — laziness buys memory and time-to-first-item, not raw throughput
  compares
    - label Generator pipeline (lazy)
      children
        - label Constant memory
          desc 20 GB CSV streams through filter, map and batch in a few KB working set
        - label ~100-200 ns per item
          desc Every resume is a Python-level frame switch
        - label Fast time-to-first-item
          desc Emits before reading the whole input
        - label Holds resources while paused
          desc with open(...) stays live; abandon it and the file handle leaks
    - label List comprehension (eager)
      children
        - label Full dataset per stage
          desc Materializing lists between stages costs the whole dataset each time
        - label ~30 ns per item
          desc C-level list iteration step, roughly 5x cheaper per step
        - label Faster raw throughput
          desc Wins million-item hot loops that fit in memory
        - label No paused frame to leak
          desc Nothing suspended holds a file descriptor
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
